# Container entrypoint/shell scripts must run under POSIX bash with an LF
# shebang. Force LF regardless of the platform's core.autocrlf so a Windows
# clone can `docker compose up --build` without the `bash\r` shebang error.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The client bundles are compiled output: `tsc` writes them with LF. On a machine with
# core.autocrlf=true every checkout would give them CRLF, so each build rewrote them and
# `git status` reported eight files as modified whose bytes were in fact identical. Pin
# the working-copy line ending to what the compiler produces.
static/dist/*.js text eol=lf

# Diagram artifacts have the same problem for the same reason: archify writes them with
# LF, and core.autocrlf=true would hand every Windows checkout a CRLF copy that a
# regeneration then reports as a rewrite. Pin them to the bytes the generator produces.
docs/diagrams/*.svg text eol=lf
